[7.535844, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' docs/PERMISSIONS.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[7.537234, "o", "# docshare access policy\r\n\r\nOwner: platform security. This is the policy every docshare endpoint must follow. Endpoint details are in `API.md`.\r\n\r\n## 1. Who is asking\r\n- Every `/api/...` request must carry `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (the token is `users.token`). A request with no\r\n  token or an unknown token gets `401`. Two endpoints need no login: `GET /api/health` and share links `GET /s/<token>`.\r\n"]
[7.537271, "o", "- A user belongs to one or more organisations (rows in `memberships`) and has one role in each: `member` or\r\n  `org_admin`.\r\n- Support staff are users with `users.is_support = 1`. They belong to no organisation and have no home organisation.\r\n\r\n## 2. The active organisation\r\n- Every request acts in one organisation, the *active organisation*: the organisation named in the `X-Org-Id` header,\r\n  or, when the header is absent, the user's home organisation (`users.home_org_id`).\r\n- A member or org_admin may only make active an organisation they belong to. If `X-Org-Id` names any other\r\n  organisation, or one that does not exist, the whole request is refused.\r\n- The caller's role is their role in the active organisation. Someone who is `member` in one organisation and\r\n  `org_admin` in another is an org_admin only while that second organisation is active.\r\n- Members and org_admins act only on folders and files of the active organisation. A file or folder of another\r\n"]
[7.537444, "o", "  organisation is refused, even if the caller also belongs to that organisation: they switch first by sending that\r\n  organisation's id in `X-Org-Id`.\r\n- Support may name any existing organisation in `X-Org-Id`; no membership is needed. For support this only chooses\r\n  what the list endpoints show. If support names an organisation that does not exist, the whole request is refused.\r\n  Without `X-Org-Id`, support's list endpoints answer `400`.\r\n\r\n## 3. What each role may do\r\n| Action | Endpoints | member | org_admin | support |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| read | `GET /api/files/<id>` | yes | yes | yes, any organisation |\r\n| download | `GET /api/files/<id>/download` | yes | yes | yes, any organisation |\r\n| thumb | `GET /api/files/<id>/thumb` | yes | yes | yes, any organisation |\r\n| list | `GET /api/files`, `GET /api/folders`, `GET /api/folders/<id>/files` | yes | yes | yes, the organisation it names |\r\n| export | `POST /api/export` | yes | yes | yes, any organisation |\r\n| rename | `PATCH /api/files/<id>` | yes | y"]
[7.537529, "o", "es | no |\r\n| share | `POST /api/files/<id>/shares`, `DELETE /api/shares/<token>` | yes | yes | no |\r\n| delete | `DELETE /api/files/<id>` | no | yes | no |\r\n| support console | `GET /api/admin/orgs` | no | no | yes |\r\n| who am I | `GET /api/me` | yes | yes | yes |\r\n\r\n- For member and org_admin, \"yes\" means: on files and folders of the active organisation only (section 2).\r\n- For support, \"any organisation\" means: any file of any organisation, whatever the active organisation is.\r\n- A list shows exactly the folders or files of the active organisation, and nothing of any other organisation.\r\n\r\n## 4. Export\r\n`POST /api/export` returns several files in one response. It is allowed only if the caller may `read` every requested\r\nid under the rules above. If even one id is not readable (a file of another organisation, a deleted file, an unknown\r\nid), the whole request is refused and the response holds no file at all.\r\n\r\n## 5. Share links\r\n- Creating a link (`POST /api/files/<id>/shares`) and revoking it (`DELETE /api/"]
[7.53759, "o", "shares/<token>`) are the `share`\r\n  action on the link's file.\r\n- Anyone who has the link can download the file with `GET /s/<token>`, without logging in, until the link is revoked\r\n  or the file is deleted. After that, or for an unknown token, the link answers `404`.\r\n\r\n## 6. Refusals\r\n- A refused request gets `403` or `404`; either is fine (404 avoids confirming that an id exists). The only other\r\n  refusal codes are `401` (section 1) and `400` (support listing without `X-Org-Id`, section 2).\r\n- A refusal holds no file data: no file contents and no name of a file the caller may not read. An error message may\r\n  repeat the id it was sent.\r\n- A refused request changes nothing: no file is renamed or deleted, no link is created or revoked.\r\n"]
[7.537681, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[7.537728, "o", "root@6dac5c62-598e-49fe-8973-206b888602c1:/app# "]
[10.419269, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/routes/files.py\n"]
[10.419591, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/routes/files.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[10.422252, "o", "\"\"\"File endpoints: list, metadata, download, rename, delete.\"\"\"\r\nfrom flask import Blueprint, Response, abort, g, jsonify, request\r\n\r\nfrom .. import db\r\nfrom ..auth import login_required, require_active_org\r\n\r\nbp = Blueprint(\"files\", __name__)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef get_file_or_404(file_id):\r\n"]
[10.422272, "o", "    row = db.query_one(f\"SELECT {db.FILE_COLUMNS}, content FROM files WHERE id = ?\", (file_id,))\r\n    if row is None:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n    return row\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/api/files\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef list_files():\r\n    org_id = require_active_org()\r\n    rows = db.query_all(f\"SELECT {db.FILE_COLUMNS} FROM files WHERE org_id = ? ORDER BY name\", (org_id,))"]
[10.422415, "o", "\r\n    return jsonify(files=[db.file_json(r) for r in rows])\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/api/files/<file_id>\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef get_file(file_id):\r\n    return jsonify(db.file_json(get_file_or_404(file_id)))\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/api/files/<file_id>/download\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef download(file_id):\r\n    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\r\n    return file_response(row)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef file_response(row):\r\n    resp = Response(bytes(row[\"content\"]), mimetype=row[\"mime_type\"])\r\n    resp.headers[\"Content-Disposition\"] = f'attachment; filename=\"{row[\"name\"]}\"'\r\n    return resp\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.patch(\"/api/files/<file_id>\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef rename(file_id):\r\n    if g.identity.role not in (\"member\", \"org_admin\"):\r\n        abort(403)\r\n    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\r\n    body = request.get_json(silent=True) or {}\r\n    name = body.get(\"name\")\r\n    if not isinstance(name, str) or not (1 <= len(name) <= 200) or \"/\" in name:\r\n        abort(400, description=\"bad_name\")\r\n    db.execute(\"UPDATE files SET name = ? WHERE id = ?\", (name, row[\"id\"]))\r\n  "]
[10.422445, "o", "  return jsonify(db.file_json(get_file_or_404(row[\"id\"])))\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.delete(\"/api/files/<file_id>\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef delete(file_id):\r\n    row = get_file_or_404(file_id)\r\n    conn = db.get_db()\r\n    conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM shares WHERE file_id = ?\", (row[\"id\"],))\r\n    conn.execute(\"DELETE FROM files WHERE id = ?\", (row[\"id\"],))\r\n    conn.commit()\r\n    return \"\", 204\r\n"]
[10.422668, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[10.422705, "o", "root@6dac5c62-598e-49fe-8973-206b888602c1:/app# "]
[10.800957, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/routes/share.py\n"]
[10.801142, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/routes/share.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[10.80248, "o", "\"\"\"Share links: create, revoke, and the public download behind /s/<token>.\"\"\"\r\nimport secrets\r\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\r\n\r\nfrom flask import Blueprint, abort, g, jsonify\r\n\r\nfrom .. import db\r\nfrom ..auth import login_required\r\nfrom .files import file_response\r\n"]
[10.802513, "o", "\r\nbp = Blueprint(\"share\", __name__)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef now_iso():\r\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.post(\"/api/files/<file_id>/shares\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef create_share(file_id):\r\n    if g.identity.role not in (\"member\", \"org_admin\"):\r\n        abort(403)\r\n    row = db.query_one(\"SELECT id FROM files WHERE id = ?\", (file_id,))\r\n    if row is None:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n"]
[10.802539, "o", "    token = secrets.token_urlsafe(18)\r\n    created = now_iso()\r\n    db.execute(\"INSERT INTO shares (token, file_id, created_by, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\",\r\n               (token, row[\"id\"], g.identity.user_id, created))\r\n    return jsonify(token=token, url=f\"/s/{token}\", file_id=row[\"id\"], created_at=created), 201\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.delete(\"/api/shares/<token>\")\r\n@login_required\r\ndef revoke_share(token):\r\n    row = db.query_one(\"SELECT s.token, f.org_id FROM shares s JOIN files f ON f.id = s.file_id WHERE s.token = ?\",\r\n                       (token,))\r\n    if row is None or row[\"org_id\"] != g.identity.org_id or g.identity.role not in (\"member\", \"org_admin\"):\r\n        abort(404)\r\n"]
[10.802561, "o", "    db.execute(\"UPDATE shares SET revoked_at = ? WHERE token = ? AND revoked_at IS NULL\", (now_iso(), token))\r\n    return \"\", 204\r\n\r\n\r\n@bp.get(\"/s/<token>\")\r\ndef public_download(token):\r\n    row = db.query_one(\"SELECT f.id, f.name, f.mime_type, f.content FROM shares s JOIN files f ON f.id = s.file_id \"\r\n                       \"WHERE s.token = ? AND s.revoked_at IS NULL\", (token,))\r\n    if row is None:\r\n        abort(404)\r\n"]
[10.802589, "o", "    return file_response(row)\r\n"]
[10.802774, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[10.802794, "o", "root@6dac5c62-598e-49fe-8973-206b888602c1:/app# "]
[11.186491, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/app.py\n"]
[11.186644, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/app.py\r\n"]
[11.186677, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[11.188183, "o", "\"\"\"Flask application factory.\"\"\"\r\nfrom flask import Flask, g, jsonify\r\nfrom werkzeug.exceptions import HTTPException\r\n\r\nfrom . import db\r\n"]
[11.188193, "o", "from .auth import login_required\r\n"]
[11.188264, "o", "from .routes import admin, export, files, folders, share, thumbs\r\n\r\n\r\ndef create_app(db_path):\r\n    app = Flask(__name__)\r\n    app.config[\"DB_PATH\"] = db_path\r\n    app.teardown_appcontext(db.close_db)\r\n    for module in (files, folders, thumbs, export, share, admin):\r\n        app.register_blueprint(module.bp)\r\n"]
[11.188305, "o", "\r\n    @app.errorhandler(HTTPException)\r\n    def http_error(exc):\r\n        code = exc.description if exc.code == 400 and exc.description and \" \" not in exc.description else exc.name\r\n        return jsonify(error=code.lower().replace(\" \", \"_\")), exc.code\r\n\r\n    @app.get(\"/api/health\")\r\n    def health():\r\n        return jsonify(ok=True)\r\n\r\n    @app.get(\"/api/me\")\r\n    @login_required\r\n    def me():\r\n        ident = g.identity\r\n        return jsonify(user={\"id\": ident.user_id, \"email\": ident.email, \"name\": ident.name,\r\n                             \"is_support\": ident.is_support},\r\n                       active_org_id=ident.org_id, role=ident.role,\r\n                       memberships=[{\"org_id\": o, \"role\": r} for o, r in sorted(ident.memberships.items())])\r\n\r\n    return app\r\n"]
[11.188509, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[11.188546, "o", "root@6dac5c62-598e-49fe-8973-206b888602c1:/app# "]
[15.534752, "i", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/auth.py\n"]
[15.534941, "o", "sed -n '1,200p' docshare/auth.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[15.536258, "o", "\"\"\"Who is calling: bearer token -> user, plus the active organisation for this request.\"\"\"\r\nimport functools\r\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\r\n\r\nfrom flask import g, jsonify, request\r\n\r\nfrom . import db\r\n"]
[15.536295, "o", "\r\n\r\n@dataclass\r\nclass Identity:\r\n    user_id: str\r\n    email: str\r\n    name: str\r\n    is_support: bool\r\n    org_id: str | None          # the active organisation for this request\r\n    role: str                   # \"member\", \"org_admin\" or \"support\"\r\n    memberships: dict = field(default_factory=dict)   # org_id -> role\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _bearer_token():\r\n"]
[15.536323, "o", "    header = request.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\")\r\n    if not header.startswith(\"Bearer \"):\r\n        return None\r\n    return header[len(\"Bearer \"):].strip() or None\r\n\r\n\r\ndef load_identity():\r\n"]
[15.536351, "o", "    token = _bearer_token()\r\n    if token is None:\r\n        return None\r\n    user = db.query_one(\"SELECT id, email, name, home_org_id, is_support FROM users WHERE token = ?\", (token,))\r\n    if user is None:\r\n        return None\r\n    memberships = {r[\"org_id\"]: r[\"role\"] for r in\r\n                   db.query_all(\"SELECT org_id, role FROM memberships WHERE user_id = ?\", (user[\"id\"],))}\r\n    # The web client only offers organisations listed by /api/me, so the header names one of the user's orgs.\r\n    org_id = request.headers.get(\"X-Org-Id\") or user[\"home_org_id\"]\r\n    if user[\"is_support\"]:\r\n        role = \"support\"\r\n    else:\r\n        role = memberships.get(org_id, \"member\")\r\n    return Identity(user_id=user[\"id\"], email=user[\"email\"], name=user[\"name\"], is_support=bool(user[\"is_support\"]),\r\n                    org_id=org_id, role=role, memberships=memberships)\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[15.536383, "o", "def login_required(view):\r\n    @functools.wraps(view)\r\n    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\r\n        ident = load_identity()\r\n        if ident is None:\r\n            return jsonify(error=\"unauthorized\"), 401\r\n        g.identity = ident\r\n"]
[15.536413, "o", "        return view(*args, **kwargs)\r\n    return wrapper\r\n\r\n\r\ndef require_active_org():\r\n    \"\"\"The active organisation id; support must name one with X-Org-Id before listing anything.\"\"\"\r\n    org_id = g.identity.org_id\r\n    if org_id is None:\r\n        from flask import abort\r\n        abort(400, description=\"x_org_id_required\")\r\n    return org_id\r\n"]
[15.536627, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[15.536648, "o", "root@6dac5c62-598e-49fe-8973-206b888602c1:/app# "]
[26.10683, "i", "apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: docshare/auth.py\n@@\n-def login_required(view):\n-    @functools.wraps(view)\n-    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):\n-        ident = load_identity()\n-        if ident is None:\n-            return jsonify(error=\"unauthorized\"), 401\n-        g.identity = ident\n-        return view(*args, **kwargs)\n-    return wrapper\n+def login_required(view):\n+    \"\"\"Require a valid bearer token and enforce the active organisation.\n+\n+    The original implementation only loaded the identity and stored it on ``g``.\n+    The permission policy (docs/PERMISSIONS.md) mandates that *every* authenticated\n+    request validates the active organisation (section 2).  By invoking\n+    ``require_active_org`` here we guarantee that the checks are performed for all\n+    routes that use ``@login_required`` – which includes every API endpoint except\n+    the health check and the public share link (both deliberately exempt).\n+    \"\"\"\n+    @functools.wraps(view)\n+    def wrapper(*args, **kwar"]
[26.106868, "i", "gs):\n+        ident = load_identity()\n+        if ident is None:\n+            return jsonify(error=\"unauthorized\"), 401\n+        g.identity = ident\n+        # Enforce active organisation validation for every protected endpoint.\n+        # ``require_active_org`` will abort with the appropriate HTTP error code\n+        # if the organisation is missing, unknown, or not permitted for the user.\n+        require_active_org()\n+        return view(*args, **kwargs)\n+    return wrapper\n@@\n-def require_active_org():\n-    \"\"\"The active organisation id; support must name one with X-Org-Id before listing anything.\"\"\"\n-    org_id = g.identity.org_id\n-    if org_id is None:\n-        from flask import abort\n-        abort(400, description=\"x_org_id_required\")\n-    return org_id\n+def require_active_org():\n+    \"\"\"Validate and return the active organisation id.\n+\n+    The policy (PERMISSIONS.md, section 2) requires:\n+    * The ``X-Org-Id`` header (or the user's home organisation) must resolve to an\n+      existing organisatio"]
[26.106993, "i", "n.\n+    * For regular users (non‑support) the organisation must be one they belong to\n+      (present in ``g.identity.memberships``).\n+    * Support staff may choose any existing organisation, but must supply the\n+      header; otherwise a ``400`` is returned.\n+\n+    The function aborts with a suitable 4xx status code when the requirements are\n+    not met and returns the validated organisation id otherwise.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    org_id = g.identity.org_id\n+    # If the header was omitted and the user is support, ``org_id`` will be ``None``.\n+    if org_id is None:\n+        from flask import abort\n+        abort(400, description=\"x_org_id_required\")\n+\n+    # Verify the organisation exists.\n+    org_row = db.query_one(\"SELECT id FROM orgs WHERE id = ?\", (org_id,))\n+    if org_row is None:\n+        # For simplicity, return a 404 – callers should not learn whether the id\n+        # exists, matching the policy's allowance of 403/404.\n+        from flask import abort\n+        abort(404, description=\"org_not_found\")\n+\n"]
[26.107035, "i", "+    # Regular (non‑support) users must belong to the organisation.\n+    if not g.identity.is_support:\n+        if org_id not in g.identity.memberships:\n+            from flask import abort\n+            abort(403, description=\"org_not_allowed\")\n+    # Support staff are allowed any existing organisation (already checked above).\n+    return org_id\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n"]
[26.107147, "o", "apply_patch <<'PATCH'\r\n"]
